# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Implementation Details

### 1. Fetched Official Documentation
- Retrieved the latest installation instructions from: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Identified Next.js App Router as the appropriate framework-specific setup

### 2. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using pnpm (the project's package manager)
- Command executed: `pnpm add @vercel/analytics`

### 3. Code Changes

#### Modified Files:
- **web/app/layout.tsx**: Added Analytics component to the root layout
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the children
  - Preserved existing code structure and formatting
  
- **web/package.json**: Updated dependencies
  - Added `"@vercel/analytics": "^2.0.1"` to dependencies

- **web/pnpm-lock.yaml**: Updated to reflect the new dependency
  - Locked file automatically updated by pnpm

### 4. Testing & Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully with `pnpm build`
  - No compilation errors
  - TypeScript validation passed
  - All 40 pages generated successfully
  
- ✅ Linting verified for modified file
  - No linting errors introduced in `app/layout.tsx`
  - Pre-existing linting errors in `.source/` directory are unrelated to this change

### 5. Implementation Notes
- Followed Next.js App Router pattern as documented by Vercel
- Analytics component placed at the end of the `<body>` tag as recommended
- No additional environment variables or configuration files required
- The Analytics component will automatically track page views once deployed to Vercel

## Next Steps
After deployment to Vercel:
1. Navigate to the Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
2. Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
3. Verify functionality by checking browser's Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`

## Files Modified
- `web/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component
- `web/package.json` - Added dependency
- `web/pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated lockfile
